    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: this dispute is escalated to a human reviewer. No refund is paid and no charge is collected or reversed while it is held. Escalation is terminal and replaces any money ruling (POL-GEN-03), so both money fields are null.\n\nWhat is common ground, and what the tribunal finds. The trip ran 23.41 km. Under POL-RD-01 the governing distance is the GPS-trace figure (EV-GPS-02855, trace_distance_km 23.41), not the rounded 23.4 km convenience copy on the trip record (EV-TRIP-02855). The booked optimal is 17.6 km (EV-TRIP-02855), so the excess is 5.81 km, or 33.01% of optimal. Both establishment tests pass (over 20% and over 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED. It is below the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gates, so no POL-RD-06 profile check, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral arises. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 184 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, zero gaps, maximum gap 0.0 s, so POL-RD-07(a)-(c) is not met and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged.\n\nWhy it escalates rather than pays. The driver explains the extra distance by a PIE closure and, in his statement, cites LTA advisory EV-ADVIS-02855-01. That artifact sits in the bundle only as a MISSING shell: admissibility status MISSING, payload null, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT (disclosed under POL-GEN-02(3)). Tested against the trip's traffic_advisory and nothing else (POL-RD-13), no advisory covers the trip window, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and the excuse carries no weight under POL-RD-08. But because the driver cited that missing identifier rather than merely asserting a closure without naming a record, POL-RD-13(1)'s express limitation applies: the clause does not narrow POL-RD-10(5) where the party does cite the missing identifier - that case still escalates. POL-RD-10(5) therefore fires (an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact missing from the pool), and its escalation is terminal.\n\nThe arithmetic that would otherwise have run, for the reviewer's benefit. The fare model is METERED (EV-FARE-02855), so POL-RD-02 would give recomputed_fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 17.6 + 0.28 x 23.8) x 1.0 surge, read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP = 24.4640; refund = charged_total 30.69 - 24.4640 = 6.2260, rounded up to SGD 6.25 (about 20.29% of charged_total, above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share). That figure does not issue on an escalation.\n\nWhat would resolve it: the actual LTA advisory for the PIE corridor in the trip window (or a record showing no closure was in force), or an independent corroborating record of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names. The reviewer should also take the driver's answer on why the advisory he cites is absent from the bundle.\n\nThe parties' claims, answered. The deviation finding itself is accepted (rider claim 1; driver claims 1 and 7). The rider's argument that the missing advisory merely makes the excuse weightless and yields the POL-RD-02 refund (rider claim 2) is rejected: it is right that POL-RD-03 cannot be run and that the excuse carries no weight under POL-RD-08, but the driver cited the missing identifier, so POL-RD-10(5) is preserved and escalates. The driver's claim that only POL-RD-10(3) is in issue (driver claim 2) is rejected on the same ground: the trace is clean, but it is POL-RD-10(5), not POL-RD-10(3), that fires. The refund arithmetic (rider claim 3; driver claim 5) is correct but does not run. No ERP, toll or surcharge correction arises (rider claim 5; driver claim 6): EV-FARE-02855 carries 0.00 ERP and no gantry or airport-surcharge lines, so POL-RD-09(2) and POL-RD-09(4) are not engaged. No exoneration under POL-RD-04 (EV-CHAT-02855 carries 0 messages, so no rider instruction and no waypoint to test), POL-RD-05 or POL-RD-12 (no endpoint amendment; vehicle type RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL) (driver claims 3 and 4). No POL-RD-06 pattern: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d 278, so neither limb is met (rider claim 6; driver claims 7 and 9). The rider-profile counters deviation_claims_60d 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated 0 add no corroboration requirement (rider claim 4; driver claim 8). The rider's POL-RD-08 burden is discharged on the matching trip_id TRP-02855 and pickup timestamp across the trip record, trace and fare breakdown. No clause on these facts produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty."
